window.LC_CHUNKS=window.LC_CHUNKS||{};window.LC_CHUNKS["university_electrical_engineering_core_en"]=window.LC_CHUNKS["university_electrical_engineering_core_en"]||{};window.LC_CHUNKS["university_electrical_engineering_core_en"][11]={"university_electrical_engineering_core_en:M11-L1":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L1\">M11-L1 – Conversion Chains and Power Profiles<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M11 – Bachelor: Energy Generation and Storage<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Bachelor · Elective<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M2&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Energy\nbalances<\/a>, <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M7&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Electrical\npower engineering<\/a>, <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M10&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Grid\nstructure<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Learning objective:<\/strong> Establish balances for\nconversion chains, integrate generation profiles and distinguish energy\nyield from available power.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>System Boundary and Energy Balance<\/h2>\n<p>Electrical energy is not a primary energy source but an energy\ncarrier. A power plant converts energy from a resource and makes it\navailable at a defined electrical connection point. We draw the system\nboundary around the entire installation, including its auxiliary\nconsumption. In steady-state operation,<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l<\/mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\">,<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"><\/mspace><msub><mi>η<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l<\/mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\">,<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mfrac><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_\\mathrm{ein}=P_\\mathrm{el,netto}+P_\\mathrm{ab},\\qquad \\eta_\\mathrm{netto}=\\frac{P_\\mathrm{el,netto}}{P_\\mathrm{ein}}.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>Here\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_\\mathrm{ab}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nincludes all other energy flows leaving the system, including useful\nheat where applicable. If the energy content of the system changes, the\ntime derivative of the stored energy must also be included. Efficiencies\ncan therefore only be compared when the system boundary and operating\nconditions are specified. For wind and PV, the reference quantity is the\nincident resource power, not fuel power.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-university-electrical-engineering-en/media/img/U_ELG_032_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Heat, wind and solar radiation are converted into electrical power through different conversion stages.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: Three conversion chains reach the AC connection via\na thermal cycle, rotating machinery or photovoltaics; each route has\ndistinct outgoing energy flows to account for.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Thermal Power Plants<\/h2>\n<p>In a steam power plant, combustion, nuclear fission or concentrated\nsolar radiation, for example, heats a working fluid. Steam expands in\nthe turbine, and the generator converts shaft power into electrical\npower. Condensation and pumping complete the cycle. The theoretical\nCarnot efficiency\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mi>/<\/mi><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ß<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1-T_\\mathrm{kalt}/T_\\mathrm{heiß}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ngives an upper bound for a reversible heat engine operating between two\nthermal reservoirs; temperatures must be expressed in kelvin. It is not\na model of the actual steam power plant.<\/p>\n<p>Example: With 100 MW of heat input, a thermal-to-mechanical cycle\nefficiency of 40%, a generator efficiency of 97% and 2 MW of electrical\nauxiliary consumption, gross and net power are 38.8 MW and 36.8 MW\nrespectively. Under unchanged operating conditions over 6 h, this\namounts to 220.8 MWh of net electrical energy. In practical models,\nefficiency, auxiliary consumption, minimum load and permissible power\nramp rate depend on the operating point. Combined heat and power makes\nuse of some of the heat that would otherwise be rejected; this is\ndistinct from electrical efficiency.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Wind, Hydropower and Photovoltaics<\/h2>\n<p>Air mass\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ<\/mi><mi>A<\/mi><mi>v<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho A v<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nflows per second through a rotor area\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>A<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nperpendicular to the airflow. Using the specific kinetic energy\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mi>/<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v^2/2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nwe obtain<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mn>1<\/mn><mn>2<\/mn><\/mfrac><mi>ρ<\/mi><mi>A<\/mi><msup><mi>v<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><\/msup><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"><\/mspace><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>η<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><msub><mi>c<\/mi><mi>P<\/mi><\/msub><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_\\mathrm{Wind}=\\frac12\\rho A v^3,\\qquad P_\\mathrm{el}=\\eta_\\mathrm{Antrieb} c_P P_\\mathrm{Wind}.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>The aerodynamic power coefficient is denoted by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>c<\/mi><mi>P<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c_P<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nFor an ideal isolated actuator disk, the Betz limit is 16/27; real\nrotors fall below it. With\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>100<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mn mathvariant=\"normal\">2<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=100\\,\\mathrm{m^2}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1.225<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/<\/mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mn mathvariant=\"normal\">3<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho=1.225\\,\\mathrm{kg/m^3}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>8<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v=8\\,\\mathrm{m/s}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c<\/mi><mi>P<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c_P=0.4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.9<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\eta_\\mathrm{Antrieb}=0.9<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe result is approximately 11.29 kW. In this model the cubic\nrelationship applies only for constant coefficients, not above rated\npower or during shutdown. A realistic plant model uses a power curve\nincluding cut-in, rated-power and cut-out regions.<\/p>\n<p>Hydropower uses a volumetric flow rate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Q<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nat a hydraulic head\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>H<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mi>η<\/mi><msub><mi>ρ<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mi>g<\/mi><mi>Q<\/mi><mi>H<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_\\mathrm{el}=\\eta\\rho_\\mathrm{Wasser}gQH<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nPhotovoltaics convert light directly into DC electrical power. An\ninverter connects the installation to an AC grid. The corresponding\ncharacteristic curves are covered in <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M11&amp;lesson=L2&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M11-L2<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Profiles, Energy and Residual Load<\/h2>\n<p>Energy is the time integral of power. For piecewise constant\nintervals,<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><msubsup><mo>∫<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mi>T<\/mi><\/msubsup><mi>P<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><munder><mo>∑<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><\/munder><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ<\/mi><msub><mi>t<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"><\/mspace><msub><mi>f<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mi>E<\/mi><mrow><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mi>T<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E=\\int_0^T P(t)\\,\\mathrm dt=\\sum_k P_k\\Delta t_k,\\qquad f_\\mathrm{Auslastung}=\\frac{E}{P_\\mathrm{Nenn}T}.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>An illustrative four-hour experiment with a rated power of 4 kW:<\/p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Hour<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Generation (kW)<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Load (kW)<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Residual load (kW)<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">2<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">2<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">4<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">1<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">−3<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">3<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">2<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">−1<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">1<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">3<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">2<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>Generation and load each amount to 8 kWh, and the generating\ninstallation’s capacity factor is 50%. Nevertheless, two intervals have\na combined deficit of 4 kWh, while a surplus of 4 kWh occurs in the\nother intervals. Only 4 kWh is used directly. The residual demand and\nsurplus must be balanced over time; the annual or daily average alone is\ninsufficient. An ideal 4 kWh storage system could absorb the surplus\nfrom both hours, but could only supply the first hour if sufficient\ninitial energy were available. Continuous supply also requires\nconsideration of power, controllability and grid limits.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Exercises with Solutions<\/h2>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">A generator delivers 12 MW for 3 h and 4 MW for another 2 h.\nDetermine the energy and average power.<br />\n<strong>Solution<\/strong> 44 MWh and 8.8 MW.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">How does wind power change when wind speed increases from 6 to 9 m/s\nwith constant coefficients?<br />\n<strong>Solution<\/strong> Factor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>9<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>6<\/mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3.375<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(9/6)^3=3.375<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\nlimits have not been taken into account.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Why can average wind power not generally be calculated from average\nwind speed?<br />\n<strong>Solution<\/strong> Because of nonlinearity, in general\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mover><msup><mi>v<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><\/msup><mo accent=\"true\">¯<\/mo><\/mover><mo>≠<\/mo><msup><mover><mi>v<\/mi><mo accent=\"true\">¯<\/mo><\/mover><mn>3<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\overline{v^3}\\ne\\overline v^3<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe frequency distribution and power curve are required.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><strong>Further reading:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M11&amp;lesson=L2&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Photovoltaics\nand Power Characteristics<\/a><\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.energy.gov/cmei/systems/concentrating-solar-thermal-power-csp-power-cycles\">U.S.\nDOE – Concentrating Solar-Thermal Power: Power Cycles<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · What are\nPower Cycles?: thermal-to-electric conversion. · Last accessed:\n2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.energy.gov/cmei/systems/windexchange/small-wind-guidebook\">U.S.\nDOE – Small Wind Guidebook<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Small Wind Guidebook, Introduction and\nHow Do Wind Turbines Work? sections: conversion of wind energy; small\nwind systems as an example. · Last accessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.energy.gov/cmei/systems/solar-photovoltaic-technology-basics\">U.S.\nDOE – Solar Photovoltaic Technology Basics<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · What Is Photovoltaic\nTechnology?: light-to-electricity conversion and module structure. ·\nLast accessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>","university_electrical_engineering_core_en:M11-L2":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L2\">M11-L2 – Photovoltaics and Power Characteristics<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M11 – Bachelor: Energy Generation and Storage<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Bachelor · Elective<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M3&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Semiconductors<\/a>,\n<a href=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M1&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Power<\/a>,\n<a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M11&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Conversion\nchains<\/a>, <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M9&amp;lesson=L3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">DC/DC\nconverters<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Learning objective:<\/strong> Interpret current-voltage\ncharacteristic curves and determine a simplified PV power profile\nincluding temperature and inverter limits.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Photoelectric Conversion<\/h2>\n<p>Absorbed photons can generate electron-hole pairs in a semiconductor.\nThe solar cell structure promotes charge separation; electrical power\ncan be delivered at the contacts when an external circuit is closed.\nUnlike a voltage source with an ohmic internal resistance, the output\ncurrent does not depend linearly on terminal voltage. Current and\nvoltage are specified as positive here using the generator sign\nconvention.<\/p>\n<p>A common steady-state single-diode model uses the photocurrent\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>I<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I_\\mathrm{ph}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\ndiode saturation current\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>I<\/mi><mn>0<\/mn><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I_0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nseries resistance\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mi>s<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand shunt resistance\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_\\mathrm{sh}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>:<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>I<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>I<\/mi><mn>0<\/mn><\/msub><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">exp<\/mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>U<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>I<\/mi><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mi>s<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><msub><mi>N<\/mi><mi>s<\/mi><\/msub><msub><mi>V<\/mi><mi>T<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><\/mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><\/mrow><mo>−<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>U<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>I<\/mi><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mi>s<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mfrac><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"><\/mspace><msub><mi>V<\/mi><mi>T<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>k<\/mi><mi>B<\/mi><\/msub><mi>T<\/mi><\/mrow><mi>q<\/mi><\/mfrac><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I=I_\\mathrm{ph}-I_0\\left[\\exp\\left(\\frac{U+IR_s}{nN_sV_T}\\right)-1\\right]-\\frac{U+IR_s}{R_\\mathrm{sh}},\\qquad V_T=\\frac{k_BT}{q}.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>N<\/mi><mi>s<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N_s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis the number of identical cells connected in series,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis the diode ideality factor, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>T<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis the absolute cell temperature. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mi>s<\/mi><\/msub><mo>≠<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_s\\ne0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nthe equation is implicit in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIts parameters must be determined for a specific module. The model does\nnot describe arbitrary partial shading without extensions for cell\ngroups and bypass diodes.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Characteristic Curve and Maximum Power Point<\/h2>\n<p>Under short-circuit conditions,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>I<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I=I_\\mathrm{sc}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\nunder open-circuit conditions,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>U<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U=U_\\mathrm{oc}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nAt both points,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>U<\/mi><mi>I<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P=UI=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nAt the maximum between these points (MPP), for a differentiable\ncharacteristic curve,<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d<\/mi><mi>P<\/mi><\/mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d<\/mi><mi>U<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mi>I<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>U<\/mi><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d<\/mi><mi>I<\/mi><\/mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d<\/mi><mi>U<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{\\mathrm dP}{\\mathrm dU}=I+U\\frac{\\mathrm dI}{\\mathrm dU}=0.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-university-electrical-engineering-en/media/img/U_ELG_033_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Schematic I-U characteristic curve and derived P-U curve with a common maximum power point.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: Power is the product of current and voltage; in this\nillustrative characteristic its maximum is at about 30.97 V, not at\neither end of the voltage axis.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<p>For illustration, we use the approximation\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>U<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>U<\/mi><mi>/<\/mi><mn>40<\/mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mn>9<\/mn><\/msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(U)=10[1-(U/40)^9]<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nA for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0<\/mn><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>U<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>40<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le U\\le40<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nV, explicitly not intended as a diode model. Differentiation gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>U<\/mi><mi>/<\/mi><mn>40<\/mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mn>9<\/mn><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1-10(U/40)^9=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\nthe MPP is at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>40<\/mn><mo>⋅<\/mo><msup><mn>0.1<\/mn><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>9<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msup><mo>≈<\/mo><mn>30.97<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U=40\\cdot0.1^{1/9}\\approx30.97<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nV,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>9<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I=9<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nA and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P<\/mi><mo>≈<\/mo><mn>278.7<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P\\approx278.7<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nW. The fill factor is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>U<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><msub><mi>I<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>≈<\/mo><mn>0.697<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_\\mathrm{mp}/(U_\\mathrm{oc}I_\\mathrm{sc})\\approx0.697<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nAn MPPT controller (Maximum Power Point Tracking) searches for a\nfavourable operating point by means of a converter. Partial shading can\nproduce several local maxima, so a simple search method does not\nnecessarily find the global maximum.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>From Irradiance and Temperature to AC Power<\/h2>\n<p>The reference power\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_\\mathrm{STC}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\napplies under standard test conditions (1000 W/m² irradiance in the\nmodule plane, 25 °C cell temperature, defined reference spectrum). As a\nsimplified linear approximation inspired by PVWatts, we use<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">max<\/mi><mo>&#8289;<\/mo><\/mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mfrac><mi>G<\/mi><mrow><mn>1000<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/<\/mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mn mathvariant=\"normal\">2<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><\/mrow><\/mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mi>γ<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><mn>25<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><msup><mrow><\/mrow><mo>∘<\/mo><\/msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><mo>,<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_\\mathrm{DC}=\\max\\left(0,P_\\mathrm{STC}\\frac{G}{1000\\,\\mathrm{W/m^2}}[1+\\gamma(T_c-25\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm C)]\\right),<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>with irradiance\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>G<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\ncell temperature\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_c<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand temperature coefficient\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>γ<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\gamma<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThis is not a complete PVWatts model; in particular, low-light\nbehaviour, spectral and optical losses and temperature dynamics are\nomitted. With fixed inverter efficiency and power limit,<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">min<\/mi><mo>&#8289;<\/mo><\/mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C<\/mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\">,<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>,<\/mo><msub><mi>η<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_\\mathrm{AC}=\\min(P_\\mathrm{AC,max},\\eta_\\mathrm{WR} P_\\mathrm{DC}).<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>For 6 kWp,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>0.004<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">−<\/mi><mn mathvariant=\"normal\">1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\gamma=-0.004\\,\\mathrm{K^{-1}}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>800<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/<\/mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mn mathvariant=\"normal\">2<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G=800\\,\\mathrm{W/m^2}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>45<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><msup><mrow><\/mrow><mo>∘<\/mo><\/msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_c=45\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm C<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe result is 4.416 kW DC and approximately 4.239 kW AC at 96% converter\nefficiency. At 1000 W/m² and 25 °C, the result would be 5.76 kW before\npower limiting; with a 5 kW inverter, 0.76 kW of potential AC power is\nlost through clipping in the simplified model. This difference is not\nequivalent to heat dissipated in the inverter.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>A Small Irradiance Profile<\/h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Quantity<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Hour 1<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Hour 2<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Hour 3<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Irradiance (W/m²)<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">400<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">800<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">1000<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cell temperature (°C)<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">30<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">45<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">50<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>DC power (kW)<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">2.352<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">4.416<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">5.400<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>AC power (kW)<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">2.258<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">4.239<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">5.000<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>The three one-hour intervals deliver a total of approximately 11.497\nkWh at the AC connection point. Actual irradiance values refer to the\ntilted module plane; horizontal weather data must be converted\ngeometrically. Cell temperature is not the same as air temperature.\nWithout this information, adding up module rated powers says little\nabout the energy yield on a particular day.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Exercises with Solutions<\/h2>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Twelve identical 400 Wp modules in series, each at 32 V and 12.5 A\nat the MPP under STC. Determine string voltage, current and power.<br />\n<strong>Solution<\/strong> 384 V, 12.5 A and 4.8 kW. This is a\ncalculation model, not design approval.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">A 6 kWp installation operates at 1000 W/m² and 60 °C;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>0.004<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">−<\/mi><mn mathvariant=\"normal\">1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\gamma=-0.004\\,\\mathrm{K^{-1}}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nDetermine the DC power.<br />\n<strong>Solution<\/strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>6<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>0.004<\/mn><mo>⋅<\/mo><mn>35<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>5.16<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">6(1-0.004\\cdot35)=5.16<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nkW.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Why is an MPP controller not a substitute for safe plant\noperation?<br />\n<strong>Solution<\/strong> Power optimisation does not automatically\naccount for cold-weather open-circuit voltage, current limits,\ninsulation, arc protection or grid requirements. These must be addressed\nseparately in the design.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><strong>Further reading:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M11&amp;lesson=L3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Comparison\nof Storage Technologies<\/a><\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.energy.gov/cmei/systems/solar-photovoltaic-technology-basics\">U.S.\nDOE – Solar Photovoltaic Technology Basics<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · What Is Photovoltaic\nTechnology?: cells, modules and arrays; partial scope. · Last accessed:\n2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://pvpmc.sandia.gov/modeling-guide/2-dc-module-iv/point-value-models/pvwatts/\">Sandia\nPVPMC – PVWatts<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · PVWatts section, equation for irradiance &gt;125\nW/m²: MPP power and temperature coefficient; note scope limitations. ·\nLast accessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://pvpmc.sandia.gov/modeling-guide/3-dc-array-iv/array-utilization/\">Sandia\nPVPMC – Array Utilization / MPPT<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Array Utilization: maximum power\npoint tracking and irradiance/cell temperature effects. · Last accessed:\n2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>","university_electrical_engineering_core_en:M11-L3":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L3\">M11-L3 – Comparison of Storage Technologies<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M11 – Bachelor: Energy Generation and Storage<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Bachelor · Elective<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M2&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Energy\nbalances<\/a>, <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M11&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Conversion\nchains<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Learning objective:<\/strong> Compare storage systems in terms\nof usable energy, power, efficiency and storage duration, explicitly\nstating the system boundaries.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Energy, Power and Storage Duration<\/h2>\n<p>Storage systems shift energy in time. They need a source for charging\nand, because of losses, return less energy than they previously\nabsorbed. Rated energy\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_N<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand maximum charging and discharging powers\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L<\/mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\">,<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_\\mathrm{L,max}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E<\/mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\">,<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_\\mathrm{E,max}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nmust be specified separately. Given the output-side usable energy\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z<\/mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\">,<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_\\mathrm{nutz,out}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe ideal duration at constant maximum output power is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z<\/mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\">,<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mi>/<\/mi><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E<\/mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\">,<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_\\mathrm{max}=E_\\mathrm{nutz,out}/P_\\mathrm{E,max}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nUsable energy may be lower than the rated value owing to temperature,\nageing or a minimum reserve.<\/p>\n<p>Electrical round-trip efficiency is<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b<\/mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\">,<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u<\/mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\">,<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mfrac><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\eta_\\mathrm{RT}=\\frac{E_\\mathrm{ab,AC}}{E_\\mathrm{zu,AC}}.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>It is defined for a complete charge/discharge sequence with the same\ninitial and final state. Auxiliary energy and standing losses must be\nincluded if they fall within the system boundary under consideration. A\nhigh value alone determines neither economic viability nor suitability\nfor long storage periods.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Electrochemical Battery<\/h2>\n<p>Electrochemical transformations take place at the electrodes during\ncharging; electrical energy is recovered during discharge. In a simple\nmodel with an approximately constant mean terminal voltage\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>U<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E<\/mi><mo>≈<\/mo><mi>U<\/mi><mi>Q<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E\\approx UQ<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nA 48 V battery with 200 Ah therefore has about 9.6 kWh of rated energy.\nWith a permissible state-of-charge window of 10 to 90%, 7.68 kWh is\ninternally usable; at 95% discharge efficiency, 7.296 kWh reaches the AC\nconnection. At an output power of 3 kW this corresponds to approximately\n2.43 h. Voltage, current, cell temperatures and state of charge limit\nactual power; cell monitoring and protection systems remain essential.\nCapacity in Ah is electric charge, not a measure of energy without a\nvoltage specification.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Pumped Storage<\/h2>\n<p>When there is surplus energy, water is pumped to an elevated\nreservoir. The potential energy available during discharge is, in\nsimplified form,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>ρ<\/mi><mi>V<\/mi><mi>g<\/mi><mi>H<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E=\\rho VgH<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nWith 1000 m³ of water, a head of 100 m, a density of 1000 kg/m³ and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>9.81<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/<\/mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mn mathvariant=\"normal\">2<\/mn><\/msup><\/mrow><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g=9.81\\,\\mathrm{m/s^2}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthis amounts to 981 MJ or 272.5 kWh of mechanical energy. A pump\nefficiency of 90% and a turbine/generator efficiency of 90% together\ngive a round-trip efficiency of 81%, without standing losses. Charging\ntherefore requires 302.78 kWh, while discharging delivers 245.25 kWh. If\nthe head varies, integration over the displaced volume is required.\nSite, reservoir volume, water flow and machine power, not just\nefficiency, limit the installation.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Hydrogen as a Chemical Storage Pathway<\/h2>\n<p>An electrolyser converts electrical energy into the chemical energy\nof hydrogen. Compression, storage and conversion back into electricity\nrequire further stages. The lower heating value (LHV) of approximately\n33.3 kWh/kg can be used to estimate the chemically stored energy. All\nefficiencies used here are consistently based on the LHV. Example: 100\nkWh of electrical input energy, 70% electrolysis efficiency, a 90%\neffective retained fraction after storage and conditioning (here\nrepresented as a stage in an energy-balance model), and a 50%\nelectricity reconversion efficiency give\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>100<\/mn><mo>⋅<\/mo><mn>0.70<\/mn><mo>⋅<\/mo><mn>0.90<\/mn><mo>⋅<\/mo><mn>0.50<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>31.5<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">100\\cdot0.70\\cdot0.90\\cdot0.50=31.5<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nkWh of electrical energy returned. This is not a claim about specific\ninstallations. A detailed model accounts for compressor electricity\nseparately, establishes a hydrogen mass balance and models\npressure-dependent losses. Direct industrial use of hydrogen has a\ndifferent useful energy output and is not equivalent to reconversion\ninto electricity.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-university-electrical-engineering-en/media/img/U_ELG_034_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Illustrative electrical energy balance for 100 kWh input in each case and the selected round-trip efficiencies.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: For 100 kWh electrical input each, the illustrative\nefficiency chains return 90.25 kWh from the battery, 81 kWh from pumped\nstorage and 31.5 kWh via hydrogen.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Comparison and Choice of System Boundary<\/h2>\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col class=\"lc-col-quarter\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-quarter\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-quarter\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-quarter\">\n<\/colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Technology<\/th>\n<th>Typical application (qualitative)<\/th>\n<th>Storage size determined by<\/th>\n<th>Power determined by<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Battery<\/td>\n<td>fast control, shifting energy by hours<\/td>\n<td>cells and usable charge window<\/td>\n<td>cells, converter, cooling<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pumped storage<\/td>\n<td>multi-hour or longer grid energy shifting<\/td>\n<td>reservoir volume and head<\/td>\n<td>pumps, turbines, conduits<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hydrogen<\/td>\n<td>longer-term storage or use as a feedstock<\/td>\n<td>vessel/cavern and operating pressure<\/td>\n<td>electrolysis and conversion back into electricity<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>The comparison values in the figure are model assumptions (battery\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>0.95<\/mn><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>=<\/mo><mn>90.25<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.95^2=90.25<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>%,\npumped storage 81%, hydrogen 31.5%), not market averages. For US\nutility-scale storage in 2019, the EIA reported average monthly\nround-trip figures of 82% for batteries and 79% for pumped storage;\nthese historical operating figures are not equivalent to specific\ncomponent efficiencies. In addition to efficiency, storage time and\npower, system design considers cycle count, costs, space, safety and\nenvironmental impacts. Energy storage systems are also not automatically\na substitute for all grid and frequency control functions.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Exercises with Solutions<\/h2>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">A storage system delivers 40 kWh at 10 kW. For how long?<br />\n<strong>Solution<\/strong> 4 h at constant output; the specified 40 kWh\nmust already represent usable output-side energy.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">How much electrical energy must a storage system with 80% round-trip\nefficiency absorb to deliver 100 kWh?<br />\n<strong>Solution<\/strong> 125 kWh with identical initial and final\nstates.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Why can hydrogen storage be of interest for long periods despite\nlower electrical energy recovery?<br />\n<strong>Solution<\/strong> Power conversion equipment and chemical\nstorage volume can be scaled differently. Whether this is advantageous\ndepends, among other factors, on site, storage losses, costs and\nintended use.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><strong>Further reading:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M11&amp;lesson=L4&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Storage\nModels and State of Charge<\/a><\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S7\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.energy.gov/cmei/water/pumped-storage-hydropower\">U.S.\nDOE – Pumped Storage Hydropower<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · What is Pumped Storage\nHydropower?: charging and discharging principle. · Last accessed:\n2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a href=\"https://www.energy.gov/cmei/fuels/hydrogen-resources\">U.S.\nDOE – Hydrogen Resources<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Introduction and Natural Gas and Other\nFossil Fuels: hydrogen production pathways; partial scope. · Last\naccessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a href=\"https://www.eia.gov/todayinEnergy/detail.php?id=46756\">U.S.\nEIA – Utility-scale batteries and pumped storage (historical operating\ndata, 2019)<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Article of 2021-02-12, paragraphs 1–2: average monthly\nround-trip efficiency of US utility-scale storage in 2019 (82%\nbatteries, 79% pumped storage). · Last accessed: 2026-11-25 · Content\nverified: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>","university_electrical_engineering_core_en:M11-L4":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L4\">M11-L4 – Storage Models and State of Charge<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M11 – Bachelor: Energy Generation and Storage<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Bachelor · Elective<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M2&amp;lesson=L7&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Computational\nexperiments<\/a>, <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M11&amp;lesson=L3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Storage\ntechnologies<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Learning objective:<\/strong> Formulate a discrete storage\nbalance, determine permissible charging and discharging power, and check\nlosses without double counting.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>State variable and sign convention<\/h2>\n<p>A battery system is described as an energy store with a lumped state\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e(t)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nin kWh. The state does not represent the entire electrochemical\ndynamics. For the balance, we consider the power at the AC connection,\nincluding the simplified converter. Charging power\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>c<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand discharging power\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nare individually non-negative quantities; the net injection at the AC\nnode is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d-c<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nFor rated energy\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_N&gt;0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe dimensionless state of charge is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C<\/mi><\/mrow><mo>=<\/mo><mi>e<\/mi><mi>/<\/mi><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{SOC}=e/E_N<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nA window of 10 to 90% means\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.1<\/mn><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_\\mathrm{min}=0.1E_N<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.9<\/mn><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_\\mathrm{max}=0.9E_N<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/p>\n<p>For a piecewise constant profile and without standing losses,<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>e<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><msub><mi>η<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/msub><msub><mi>c<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mfrac><msub><mi>d<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><msub><mi>η<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/msub><\/mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_{k+1}=e_k+\\eta_c c_k\\Delta t-\\frac{d_k}{\\eta_d}\\Delta t.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>η<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\eta_c<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>η<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\eta_d<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nlie in the interval\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(0,1]<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand refer to the AC connection. With\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Delta t<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nin hours and power in kW, the result is in kWh. Discharging requires\nmore energy internally than reaches the connection. If an hourly\nretention factor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>r<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\n(0 to 1) is used for standing losses, one possible discrete model is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msup><mi>r<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/msup><msub><mi>e<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><msub><mi>η<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/msub><msub><mi>c<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>d<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><mi>/<\/mi><msub><mi>η<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_{k+1}=r^{\\Delta t/(1\\,\\mathrm h)}e_k+\\eta_c c_k\\Delta t-d_k\\Delta t/\\eta_d<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\nthe standing losses are applied to the initial energy. For losses and\nenergy flows distributed continuously over the interval, the exact\ndifferential equation model must be integrated. In the following\nexample,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-university-electrical-engineering-en/media/img/U_ELG_035_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Energy flow at the AC node with charging and discharging efficiencies, state-of-charge window and loss paths.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: Charging increases the internal energy only by its\nefficiency-adjusted share; during discharge, the internal energy removed\nexceeds the AC energy delivered because of losses.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Deriving power limits from energy bounds<\/h2>\n<p>For charging only\n(<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>),\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>≤<\/mo><msub><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_{k+1}\\le e_\\mathrm{max}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nmust hold; for discharging only\n(<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>),\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>≥<\/mo><msub><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_{k+1}\\ge e_\\mathrm{min}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nmust hold. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Delta t&gt;0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthis gives<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">min<\/mi><mo>&#8289;<\/mo><\/mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L<\/mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\">,<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>,<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><mi>e<\/mi><\/mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"><\/mspace><mi>d<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">min<\/mi><mo>&#8289;<\/mo><\/mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E<\/mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\">,<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>,<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>e<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><msub><mi>η<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c\\le\\min\\left(P_\\mathrm{L,max},\\frac{e_\\mathrm{max}-e}{\\eta_c\\Delta t}\\right),\\qquad d\\le\\min\\left(P_\\mathrm{E,max},\\frac{(e-e_\\mathrm{min})\\eta_d}{\\Delta t}\\right).<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>The limit is applied before updating the state. Clipping the state\nafterwards would cause the energy not absorbed or not delivered to\ndisappear without a corresponding balance entry. With standing losses,\nthe limit must refer to the state remaining after those losses; if the\nminimum reserve is thereby breached, the model needs a\nreserve-maintenance strategy or an explicit constraint violation report.\nBelow, we assume a permissible initial state and do not allow\nsimultaneous charging and discharging\n(<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">cd=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>).<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Worked example at the consumer node<\/h2>\n<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_N=10<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nkWh,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_\\mathrm{min}=1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nkWh,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>9<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_\\mathrm{max}=9<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nkWh, both power limits be 3 kW and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>η<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.95<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\eta_c=\\eta_d=0.95<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe initial energy is 6 kWh. First, there is a surplus of 4 kW for 2 h.\nPower is limited to 3 kW, while the available storage capacity further\nlimits the average charging power to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>0.95<\/mn><mo>⋅<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1.578947<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3/(0.95\\cdot2)=1.578947<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nkW. Alternatively, with a time-constant connection model, charging at 3\nkW can continue until the limit is reached and then stop. The energy\nabsorbed remains 3.157895 kWh, with 4.842105 kWh of surplus remaining.\nThe final state is 9 kWh.<\/p>\n<p>A deficit of 4 kW for 3 h follows. Energy and power bounds give an\naverage discharge power of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">min<\/mi><mo>&#8289;<\/mo><\/mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>8<\/mn><mo>⋅<\/mo><mn>0.95<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>3<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2.533333<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\min(3,8\\cdot0.95/3)=2.533333<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nkW. The store supplies 7.6 kWh, and 4.4 kWh must be supplied elsewhere.\nThe final state is 1 kWh.<\/p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Energy balance entry<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Charging (kWh)<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Discharging (kWh)<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>AC energy<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">3.157895<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">7.600000<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Change in internal energy<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">+3.000000<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">−8.000000<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Loss<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0.157895<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0.400000<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>The total energy loss is 0.557895 kWh. Since the initial energy is 5\nkWh greater than the final energy, comparing input and output energy\nover this period does not yield the round-trip efficiency. The correct\nbalance is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ<\/mi><mi>e<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_c-E_d=\\Delta e+E_\\mathrm{Verlust}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Operating strategy and model limitations<\/h2>\n<p>For a pure self-consumption strategy, directly available generation\nis used by the load first. Only the remaining surplus charges the store,\nand only the remaining deficit is supplied from it. The grid or another\nsource covers the remainder. A predictive strategy might maintain a\nminimum reserve for later islanded operation or operate the store\ndifferently under dynamic tariffs. The energy balance is unchanged; only\nthe choice of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>c<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nchanges. An electrical equivalent circuit with internal resistance,\nvoltage dependence and ageing would be necessary to predict cell\ncurrents or thermal effects. For the operational planning in <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M11&amp;lesson=L5&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M11-L5<\/a>,\nthe lumped model is sufficient.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Exercises with solutions<\/h2>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>8.5<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e=8.5<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nkWh,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>9<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_\\mathrm{max}=9<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nkWh,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.95<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\eta_c=0.95<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.5<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Delta t=0.5<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nh. What limits the average power?<br />\n<strong>Solution<\/strong> The energy bound gives 1.05263 kW; the\nhardware limit also applies.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">With\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e=2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nkWh,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_\\mathrm{min}=1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nkWh and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.95<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\eta_d=0.95<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n2 kW is requested for one hour. Determine the maximum energy delivered\nif sufficient discharge power is available.<br />\n<strong>Solution<\/strong> 0.95 kWh; 1.05 kWh remains unmet.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Why must a simulation not simply reset the state to within the\npermissible window?<br />\n<strong>Solution<\/strong> Excess energy must be accounted for as surplus\nnot absorbed or demand not met; otherwise the calculation violates\nconservation of energy.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><strong>Further reading:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M11&amp;lesson=L5&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Case study:\nElectricity Supply with Storage<\/a><\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://docs.pypsa.org/latest/user-guide/optimization/storage/\">PyPSA\n– Storage: Energy balance and storage bounds<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Storage Units,\nStorageUnit-energy_balance equation: state-of-charge balance. · Last\naccessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a href=\"https://www.eia.gov/todayinEnergy/detail.php?id=46756\">U.S.\nEIA – Utility-scale batteries and pumped storage (historical operating\ndata for 2019)<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Article of 2021-02-12, paragraphs 1–2: definition\nand historical operating values of round-trip efficiency; not a source\nfor the specific state balance. · Last accessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>","university_electrical_engineering_core_en:M11-L5":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L5\">M11-L5 – Case Study: Electricity Supply with Storage<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M11 – Bachelor: Energy Generation and Storage<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Bachelor · Elective<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M11&amp;lesson=L2&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Photovoltaics<\/a>,\n<a href=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M11&amp;lesson=L4&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Storage\nmodel<\/a>, <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M2&amp;lesson=L7&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Computational\nexperiments<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Learning objective:<\/strong> Simulate a PV, load and storage\nsystem over 48 hours, compare variants on a consistent energy-balance\nbasis, and explain the influence of energy and power bounds.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Modelling question and boundary conditions<\/h2>\n<p>A grid-connected consumer aims to increase the proportion of solar\nenergy consumed locally. We investigate the effects of rated energy and\ncharging/discharging power in an AC-coupled storage system. The two days\nare synthetic, not measured weather or household data. Day 1 is sunny;\nday 2 has the same profile shape with 35% of the generation power. The\nload is the same on both days. The PV values already refer to the AC\nside, so no additional inverter efficiency is applied. Storage losses\nare included in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>η<\/mi><mi>d<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.95<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\eta_c=\\eta_d=0.95<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe grid is available without limits in both directions. Standby\nconsumption, ageing, costs, reactive power, temperature and grid\ndynamics are neglected. All stores start at a state of charge of 10% and\nmay be charged to 90%. The case without storage has\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mi>N<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_N=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\na percentage SOC is undefined in that case.<\/p>\n<p>The operating rule in each interval is to supply the load directly\nfrom PV, store surplus up to the energy or power limit, and export the\nremainder. If there is a deficit, supply it from the store and import\nthe remaining load from the grid.<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">min<\/mi><mo>&#8289;<\/mo><\/mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>,<\/mo><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"><\/mspace><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><mi>d<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_\\mathrm{direkt}=\\min(P_\\mathrm{PV},P_\\mathrm{Last}),\\qquad\nP_\\mathrm{Netzbezug}=P_\\mathrm{Last}-P_\\mathrm{direkt}-d,<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>P<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><mi>c<\/mi><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_\\mathrm{Export}=P_\\mathrm{PV}-P_\\mathrm{direkt}-c.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>The limits from M11-L4 determine\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>c<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nSince charging uses only surplus generation, all delivered energy above\nthe initial reserve in this experiment comes from PV. We define the\nenergy-balance degree of self-sufficiency as\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mi>/<\/mi><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a=1-E_\\mathrm{Netzbezug}/E_\\mathrm{Last}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe PV self-consumption fraction\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mi>/<\/mi><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b=1-E_\\mathrm{Export}/E_\\mathrm{PV}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nalso includes storage losses and any PV energy remaining in the store.\nThe two metrics are therefore different.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Reproducible simulation<\/h2>\n<p>The hourly values in kW are given in full in the following code. It\nrequires only Python 3; the 15-minute variant repeats each hourly value\nfour times. Positive power quantities avoid changing sign conventions\nfor import and export. In each interval, the stored energy is updated\nand then the energy quantities are summed.<\/p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb1\"><pre\nclass=\"sourceCode python\"><code class=\"sourceCode python\"><span id=\"cb1-1\"><a href=\"#cb1-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>load <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> [<span class=\"fl\">.6<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">.5<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">.5<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">.5<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">.5<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">.7<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">1.2<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">1.8<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">1.1<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">.8<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">.7<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">.8<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">1.0<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">.8<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">.7<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">.8<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">1.0<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">1.5<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">2.2<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">2.5<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">1.8<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">1.2<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">.9<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">.7<\/span>]<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-2\"><a href=\"#cb1-2\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>solar <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> [<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">.1<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">.5<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">1.2<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">2.4<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">3.5<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">4.2<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">4.5<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">4.2<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">3.5<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">2.5<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">1.4<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">.5<\/span>,<span class=\"fl\">.1<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>]<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-3\"><a href=\"#cb1-3\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>pv <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> solar <span class=\"op\">+<\/span> [<span class=\"fl\">0.35<\/span><span class=\"op\">*<\/span>p <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> p <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> solar]<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-4\"><a href=\"#cb1-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>load <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> load<span class=\"op\">*<\/span><span class=\"dv\">2<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-5\"><a href=\"#cb1-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-6\"><a href=\"#cb1-6\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> simulate(cap, limit, dt<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-7\"><a href=\"#cb1-7\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    eta_c <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> eta_d <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"fl\">.95<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-8\"><a href=\"#cb1-8\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    lo, hi <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"fl\">.1<\/span><span class=\"op\">*<\/span>cap, <span class=\"fl\">.9<\/span><span class=\"op\">*<\/span>cap<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-9\"><a href=\"#cb1-9\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    e <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> e0 <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> lo<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-10\"><a href=\"#cb1-10\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    totals <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">dict<\/span>(pv<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"fl\">0.<\/span>, load<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"fl\">0.<\/span>, direct<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"fl\">0.<\/span>, charge<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"fl\">0.<\/span>, discharge<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"fl\">0.<\/span>, grid<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"fl\">0.<\/span>, export<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"fl\">0.<\/span>, loss<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"fl\">0.<\/span>)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-11\"><a href=\"#cb1-11\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    trace <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> [e]<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-12\"><a href=\"#cb1-12\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> g, l <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">zip<\/span>(pv, load):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-13\"><a href=\"#cb1-13\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> _ <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">range<\/span>(<span class=\"bu\">round<\/span>(<span class=\"dv\">1<\/span><span class=\"op\">/<\/span>dt)):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-14\"><a href=\"#cb1-14\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            direct <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">min<\/span>(g,l)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-15\"><a href=\"#cb1-15\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            c <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">min<\/span>(g<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>direct, limit, <span class=\"bu\">max<\/span>(<span class=\"fl\">0.<\/span>,(hi<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>e)<span class=\"op\">/<\/span>(eta_c<span class=\"op\">*<\/span>dt)))<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-16\"><a href=\"#cb1-16\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            d <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">min<\/span>(l<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>direct, limit, <span class=\"bu\">max<\/span>(<span class=\"fl\">0.<\/span>,(e<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>lo)<span class=\"op\">*<\/span>eta_d<span class=\"op\">/<\/span>dt))<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-17\"><a href=\"#cb1-17\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            e <span class=\"op\">+=<\/span> (eta_c<span class=\"op\">*<\/span>c<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>d<span class=\"op\">/<\/span>eta_d)<span class=\"op\">*<\/span>dt<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-18\"><a href=\"#cb1-18\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            values <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">dict<\/span>(pv<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>g, load<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>l, direct<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>direct, charge<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>c, discharge<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>d,<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-19\"><a href=\"#cb1-19\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>                          grid<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>l<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>direct<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>d, export<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>g<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>direct<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>c,<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-20\"><a href=\"#cb1-20\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>                          loss<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>(<span class=\"dv\">1<\/span><span class=\"op\">-<\/span>eta_c)<span class=\"op\">*<\/span>c<span class=\"op\">+<\/span>(<span class=\"dv\">1<\/span><span class=\"op\">/<\/span>eta_d<span class=\"op\">-<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>)<span class=\"op\">*<\/span>d)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-21\"><a href=\"#cb1-21\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> key, val <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> values.items():<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-22\"><a href=\"#cb1-22\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>                totals[key] <span class=\"op\">+=<\/span> val<span class=\"op\">*<\/span>dt<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-23\"><a href=\"#cb1-23\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            <span class=\"cf\">assert<\/span> lo<span class=\"op\">-<\/span><span class=\"fl\">1e-9<\/span> <span class=\"op\">&lt;=<\/span> e <span class=\"op\">&lt;=<\/span> hi<span class=\"op\">+<\/span><span class=\"fl\">1e-9<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">and<\/span> c<span class=\"op\">*<\/span>d <span class=\"op\">&lt;<\/span> <span class=\"fl\">1e-9<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-24\"><a href=\"#cb1-24\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            trace.append(e)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-25\"><a href=\"#cb1-25\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    totals[<span class=\"st\">&#39;delta&#39;<\/span>] <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> e<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>e0<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-26\"><a href=\"#cb1-26\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">assert<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">abs<\/span>(totals[<span class=\"st\">&#39;pv&#39;<\/span>]<span class=\"op\">+<\/span>totals[<span class=\"st\">&#39;grid&#39;<\/span>]<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>totals[<span class=\"st\">&#39;load&#39;<\/span>]<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>totals[<span class=\"st\">&#39;export&#39;<\/span>]<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>totals[<span class=\"st\">&#39;loss&#39;<\/span>]<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>totals[<span class=\"st\">&#39;delta&#39;<\/span>]) <span class=\"op\">&lt;<\/span> <span class=\"fl\">1e-9<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-27\"><a href=\"#cb1-27\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> totals, trace<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-28\"><a href=\"#cb1-28\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-29\"><a href=\"#cb1-29\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> cap, limit <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> [(<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>),(<span class=\"dv\">5<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">3<\/span>),(<span class=\"dv\">10<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">3<\/span>),(<span class=\"dv\">15<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">3<\/span>),(<span class=\"dv\">10<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>)]:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-30\"><a href=\"#cb1-30\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    s, trace <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> simulate(cap,limit)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-31\"><a href=\"#cb1-31\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    fine, _ <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> simulate(cap,limit,<span class=\"fl\">.25<\/span>)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-32\"><a href=\"#cb1-32\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">assert<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">all<\/span>(<span class=\"bu\">abs<\/span>(s[k]<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>fine[k]) <span class=\"op\">&lt;<\/span> <span class=\"fl\">1e-9<\/span> <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> k <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> s)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-33\"><a href=\"#cb1-33\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"bu\">print<\/span>(cap,limit, {k:<span class=\"bu\">round<\/span>(v,<span class=\"dv\">4<\/span>) <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> k,v <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> s.items()}, <span class=\"bu\">round<\/span>(<span class=\"dv\">100<\/span><span class=\"op\">*<\/span>(<span class=\"dv\">1<\/span><span class=\"op\">-<\/span>s[<span class=\"st\">&#39;grid&#39;<\/span>]<span class=\"op\">/<\/span>s[<span class=\"st\">&#39;load&#39;<\/span>]),<span class=\"dv\">2<\/span>))<\/span><\/code><\/pre><\/div>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Results and balance check<\/h2>\n<p>Over 48 hours, the load consumes 49.60 kWh and PV generation amounts\nto 38.61 kWh. Of this, 15.83 kWh is used directly. During the first\nnight before sunrise, no storage system can supply energy from PV\nalready generated in this experiment. All variants finish at their\ninitial energy, making the cases directly comparable.<\/p>\n<table class=\"lc-table-width-99\">\n<colgroup>\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-16\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-16\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-16\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-16\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-16\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-16\">\n<\/colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Rated energy (kWh)<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Limit (kW)<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Grid import (kWh)<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Export (kWh)<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Loss (kWh)<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Self-sufficiency (%)<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">33.77<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">22.78<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">31.92<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"text-right\">5<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">3<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">27.19<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">15.49<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0.71<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">45.18<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"text-right\">10<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">3<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">23.39<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">11.28<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">1.12<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">52.84<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"text-right\">15<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">3<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">19.59<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">7.07<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">1.53<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">60.50<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"text-right\">10<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">1<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">24.22<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">12.20<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">1.03<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">51.17<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-university-electrical-engineering-en/media/img/U_ELG_036_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Hourly PV generation and load values and the state of charge of the 10 kWh store with a 3 kW power limit.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: In the 48-hour example, a 10 kWh storage device with\na 3 kW power limit shifts surplus PV generation over time; generation,\nload and stored energy are shown separately.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<p>For 10 kWh / 3 kW, the unrounded calculation gives 11.5010526316 kWh\nof charging energy and 10.3797 kWh of discharging energy; the actual\nround-trip efficiency is 90.25%. A total of 27.3311 kWh of PV energy\nremains behind the grid connection (used directly or charged into the\nstore). The corresponding PV self-consumption fraction is approximately\n70.79%, but the degree of self-sufficiency is only 52.84%. The two-sided\nbalance check is<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><msub><mi>E<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ<\/mi><mi>e<\/mi><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_\\mathrm{PV}+E_\\mathrm{Netzbezug}=E_\\mathrm{Last}+E_\\mathrm{Export}+E_\\mathrm{Verlust}+\\Delta e.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>Using rounded table values:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>38.61<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>23.39<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>49.60<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>11.28<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1.12<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>62.00<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">38.61+23.39=49.60+11.28+1.12=62.00<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nkWh. The calculation checks the equation before rounding. The total\nenergy supplied by PV and storage to the load is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>15.83<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>10.3797<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>26.2097<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">15.83+10.3797=26.2097<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nkWh. The 15-minute calculation gives the same energy totals in this\npiecewise constant model; this demonstrates consistency of the interval\nmodel but does not prove the physical validity of the hourly\nprofile.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Interpretation and extension<\/h2>\n<p>In the example, the 15 kWh store increases self-sufficiency compared\nwith 10 kWh, but even this store does not achieve complete autonomy.\nEven without exports and losses, with identical initial and final stored\nenergy, the deficit is at least the difference between consumption and\ngeneration: 10.99 kWh. Greater storage capacity alone cannot close this\nenergy gap. The 1 kW variant can shift less power during surplus and\ndeficit hours; despite the same rated energy, grid import increases. A\ngenuinely optimal size depends on many longer profiles, weather, usage\nbehaviour, tariffs, investment and ageing costs. Grid connection power\nand the ability to operate in island mode are separate requirements, not\nconsequences of the degree of self-sufficiency calculated here\nalone.<\/p>\n<p>As a project task, add a week with widely varying generation,\nintroduce a retention factor for standing losses and investigate a range\nof capacities. Choose comparable initial and final states or explicitly\naccount for the state change. Document the model assumptions, energy\nbounds and metrics in accordance with <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M8&amp;lesson=L5&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M8-L5<\/a>.\nThe temporal resolution must be justified using the actual power\nprofiles, not merely convergence when hourly values are repeated.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Exercises with solutions<\/h2>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">How much grid import does the 10 kWh / 3 kW variant save compared\nwith the case without storage?<br />\n<strong>Solution<\/strong> 10.3797 kWh; this corresponds to the energy\ndelivered by the store because direct use does not change.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Why does export decrease by more energy than import?<br />\n<strong>Solution<\/strong> 11.5011 kWh is charged, but only 10.3797 kWh\nis discharged. The difference of 1.1214 kWh is lost.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Can the system with 15 kWh of storage operate autonomously if the\ngrid connection is removed?<br />\n<strong>Solution<\/strong> No. For the selected profiles and identical\ninitial and final states, there is a fundamental shortfall of at least\n10.99 kWh; charging and discharging power are also limited. Without the\ngrid, unmet load must be reported explicitly as such.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><strong>Further reading:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;page=study-path&amp;section=S3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Study\npathway – further modules<\/a><\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.energy.gov/cmei/systems/solar-photovoltaic-system-design-basics\">U.S.\nDOE – Solar Photovoltaic System Design Basics<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Solar Photovoltaic\nSystem Design Basics, introduction and Mounting Structures: system\ncomponents and generation conditions; further reading. · Last accessed:\n2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://docs.pypsa.org/latest/user-guide/optimization/storage/\">PyPSA\n– Storage: Energy balance and storage bounds<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Storage Units,\nStorageUnit-energy_balance equation: storage balance in the case model.\n· Last accessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://pvpmc.sandia.gov/modeling-guide/2-dc-module-iv/point-value-models/pvwatts/\">Sandia\nPVPMC – PVWatts<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · PVWatts section: irradiance and cell temperature\nas inputs to a PV power model; further reading, not the origin of\nsynthetic AC profiles. · Last accessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>"};
